# playpick cell: mode=raid boss=whisper spec=warrior:protection style=mash
# size=10 difficulty=normal view=390x844,touch save=fresh
#
# What is new here: mash-style has never been paired with warrior:protection
# on record (grep of sessions.jsonl for style=mash + spec=warrior:protection
# is empty), and the one prior warrior:protection pull of The Last Whisper
# (2026-09-28, idle style, 844x390 landscape) never pressed anything at all.
# mash round-robins ability slots 1-5 with no movement of its own
# (scripts/playbot.ts: mash is absent from every steering branch), so a tank
# under mash stands on its spawn point and randomly presses its own kit
# instead of using cooldowns with any judgment -- a different failure shape
# than idle's "never touch a slot" for the same class/boss/size/difficulty
# pairing, and the first read on whether a tank's own rotation (taunt/block
# slots) does anything useful when fired blind. The probe
# (2026-09-30-1-probe.play) confirmed the roster screen's tile name after a
# direct #b=whisper&s=10&h=0 link is "class:warrior:protection" (2026-09-29-2's
# script named its tile with no "class:" prefix -- that looks like a mistake
# in that script, not a real difference between sessions, since the probe run
# just now shows every tile on this screen carrying the "class:" prefix).
open #b=whisper&s=10&h=0
shot roster
targets
tap class:warrior:protection
shot picked
targets
tap pull
shot pulling
waitscreen fight 15
state

play mash 90
shot mid1
state
says
bill

play mash 90
shot mid2
state
says
bill

play mash 60
shot outcome
state
says
bill

# outcome.png caught enrage at 2s left (bossHp 41%, heroHp 969/2790, hitsPerMin
# under 2 the entire fight) -- extending to see whether enrage actually wipes
# the raid or is a lesser penalty, since no session on record has run a mash
# pull past a timed enrage on this boss.
play mash 40
shot enrage-check
state
says
bill
